@meta
id: 18-14
title: The argument list
chapter: 18
type: lesson
skills: arglist
par: 97
minutes: 6
vscode: open each file from the sidebar in turn
open: README.md

@brief
Refunds are getting their own status. `OrderStatus` gains
`'REFUNDED'` at the end of the union, and the resolver's `cancelOrder`
must pass `'REFUNDED'` as a second argument to `orderProvider.cancel`.
Two of the four order files change; the provider and repository do not.

When you started vim with several files on the command line, chapter 16
showed you `:bn` walking through them. That list of files is the
argument list, and it is not fixed at startup. `:args src/domain/order/*.ts`
replaces it with every match of the glob and opens the first one.
`:next` and `:prev` step through it, `:first` and `:last` jump to the
ends, and `:args` on its own shows where you are.

The README stays as it is.

@keys
| `:args glob` | set the argument list from a glob, open the first |
| `:args` | show the list, current file in brackets |
| `:n` `:next` | next file in the list |
| `:prev` `:N` | previous |
| `:first` `:last` | either end |
| `:wn` | write, then next |
| `:wqa` | write everything, quit |

@hints
`:args src/domain/order/*.ts` gives you four files in alphabetical
order. The entity is first.
--
Edit the entity, then `:wn` to write it and move on. `:n` skips a file
you do not need. The resolver is last, so `:last` gets there in one.
--
Entity: `G$i | 'REFUNDED'` Esc. `:wn`. `:last`. Resolver: `/cancel(`
Enter, `f)`, `i, 'REFUNDED'` Esc. `:wq`.

@solution
    :args src/domain/order/*.ts<Enter>
    G$ i | 'REFUNDED' <Esc> :wn<Enter>
    :last<Enter> /cancel(<Enter> f) i, 'REFUNDED' <Esc> :wq<Enter>

The argument list is a to-do list of files. Buffers accumulate
everything you have ever opened; the arglist holds only what you meant
to work through, in the order you meant to do it. `:args` shows it with
the current one in square brackets, so you always know how far along
you are.

The same glob works for `:argadd`, which appends without replacing. And
in chapter 25, `:argdo` runs a command over every file in the list,
which is when the arglist stops being a convenience and becomes a tool.

`:wq` on the last file quits cleanly. `:wq` with files still unvisited
gets you E173, "more files to edit", which is vim making sure you did
not forget one. `:wqa` overrides it.

@start README.md
# Orders service

Order statuses: PENDING, SHIPPED, CANCELLED, and now REFUNDED once the
payment gateway confirms the money has gone back.

@start src/domain/order/order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@expected src/domain/order/order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED' | 'REFUNDED';

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { OrderStatus } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
  ) {}

  public async cancel(id: string, status: OrderStatus = 'CANCELLED') {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status },
    });
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Order as OrderRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Order } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderRepository extends BaseRepository<OrderRecord, Order> {
  public toEntity(record: OrderRecord): Order {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      customerId: record.customerId,
      status: record.status,
      total: record.total,
    };
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id, 'REFUNDED');
  }
}
